flowchart TB
  accTitle: Four evidence-led architecture levels
  accDescr: Start with a flat library, then add static routing, filtered retrieval, and governed runtime controls only when measured local pressure justifies the next level. Every promotion preserves a rollback path.

  E["<b>Promotion evidence</b><br/>Task outcomes · routing quality · privacy<br/>Latency · cost · drift"]
  R["<b>Safety boundary</b><br/>Shadow the candidate<br/>Keep the last known-good level runnable"]

  subgraph levels["Choose the smallest level that clears the measured constraint"]
    direction LR
    L0["<b>Level 0 · Flat</b><br/>Small, simple library<br/>Progressive resources"]
    L1["<b>Level 1 · Route</b><br/>Stable task domains<br/>Static routing compiler"]
    L2["<b>Level 2 · Retrieve</b><br/>Catalog or overlap pressure<br/>Filter, search, inspect"]
    L3["<b>Level 3 · Govern</b><br/>Dynamic or higher-risk use<br/>Policy, telemetry, lifecycle"]

    L0 --> L1 --> L2 --> L3
  end

  E -.-> levels
  levels -.-> R

  classDef level fill:#20808D,stroke:#187078,color:#FFFFFF,stroke-width:2px;
  classDef evidence fill:#E8F4F6,stroke:#187078,color:#13343B,stroke-width:2px;
  classDef rollback fill:#FFF3E0,stroke:#C47530,color:#13343B,stroke-width:2px;

  class L0,L1,L2,L3 level;
  class E evidence;
  class R rollback;

  style levels fill:#FFFFFF,stroke:#CBD5DA,stroke-width:1px
